WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.578
The same night that Nello had visited Alois at her window, there was a fire at the mill.

2
00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:12.847
The fire engines came from Antwerp, rushing through the snow.

3
00:00:12.848 --> 00:00:16.585
Many villagers also came to help.

4
00:00:16.586 --> 00:00:21.401
Nello, too, came to save the mill from burning.

5
00:00:21.402 --> 00:00:26.224
The outer buildings and many cornfields were destroyed.

6
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:30.996
Thankfully, the mill itself and the house were unharmed.

7
00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:35.113
The miller was insured and would lose nothing.

8
00:00:35.114 --> 00:00:40.225
Nevertheless, he was furious.

9
00:00:40.226 --> 00:00:45.249
The miller declared that the fire was not an accident.

10
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:49.585
He insisted that someone had set fire to the mill.

11
00:00:49.586 --> 00:00:53.922
When he saw Nello helping put out the fire, he said,

12
00:00:53.923 --> 00:00:56.894
"I saw you here in the night.

13
00:00:56.896 --> 00:01:03.565
I think you know something about the fire!"

14
00:01:03.566 --> 00:01:07.169
Nello listened to Master Cogez.

15
00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.462
He was too shocked to reply.

16
00:01:10.463 --> 00:01:16.408
"How could anyone say such a thing except as a joke?" Nello thought.

17
00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:21.017
But clearly, the miller was not joking.

18
00:01:21.018 --> 00:01:26.829
The next day, the miller told his neighbors that he suspected Nello.

19
00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:29.914
People in the village gossiped.

20
00:01:29.915 --> 00:01:36.958
They said Nello was angry with the miller because he was not allowed to see Alois.

21
00:01:36.959 --> 00:01:43.549
In their hearts, the villagers didn't really believe that Nello had lit the fire.

22
00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:48.482
But the miller was powerful, and the villagers were poor.

23
00:01:48.483 --> 00:01:52.918
They didn't dare question the miller's opinion.

24
00:01:52.919 --> 00:01:59.384
So the villagers no longer smiled at Nello or said hello.

25
00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:06.134
When Nello and Patrasche picked up their milk, the villagers just looked at the ground.

26
00:02:06.135 --> 00:02:09.906
Nello could do nothing.

27
00:02:09.907 --> 00:02:16.044
"You are very cruel to Nello," the miller's wife said to her husband.

28
00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:17.836
"He is innocent.

29
00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:22.617
Maybe Nello was upset that he couldn't see Alois anymore.

30
00:02:22.618 --> 00:02:25.031
But he is a good boy.

31
00:02:25.032 --> 00:02:28.755
He would never set fire to our house."

32
00:02:28.756 --> 00:02:34.276
When he thought over his wife's words, the miller felt she was right.

33
00:02:34.277 --> 00:02:37.925
But the miller was a stubborn man.

34
00:02:37.926 --> 00:02:43.113
Once he had said something, he would not change his mind.

35
00:02:43.114 --> 00:02:47.981
Nello, for his part, never complained about the miller.

36
00:02:47.982 --> 00:02:53.134
To Patrasche only, he sighed a little about what had happened.

37
00:02:53.135 --> 00:03:00.157
But then he thought, "If my picture wins, he'll be sorry, perhaps."

38
00:03:00.158 --> 00:03:05.494
Still, it was a difficult time for the 15-year-old boy.

39
00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:09.919
He had done nothing wrong, and he was a good young man.

40
00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.604
Yet it seemed as if the whole world were against him.

41
00:03:15.605 --> 00:03:18.771
Winters in Flanders are hard.

42
00:03:18.772 --> 00:03:23.395
In the village, there was a lot of snow and little food.

43
00:03:23.396 --> 00:03:29.617
Usually, the villagers helped each other out, but this winter was different.

44
00:03:29.618 --> 00:03:36.418
No one came to visit Nello's grandfather or left extra milk at their door.

45
00:03:36.419 --> 00:03:39.215
And then, it got worse.

46
00:03:39.216 --> 00:03:45.837
A man from Antwerp started to deliver milk with a large wagon and a mule.

47
00:03:45.838 --> 00:03:50.714
Most villagers stopped giving their milk to Nello to deliver.

48
00:03:50.715 --> 00:03:56.479
Instead of twenty customers, now Nello had only four.

49
00:03:56.480 --> 00:04:00.268
Patrasche did not understand the change.

50
00:04:00.269 --> 00:04:05.687
In the mornings, he would stop, as always, at all the familiar gates.

51
00:04:05.688 --> 00:04:08.630
Now the gates stayed closed.

52
00:04:08.631 --> 00:04:20.561
Patrasche had less milk to carry in the green cart, and Nello had fewer coins in his pocket.

